// Declares a reactive context: `context #name(default)` binds `name`, and
// `name(value) { ... }` overrides it for a subtree. A context is ambient
// because the form that declares one has to be available wherever a package
// declares state, and the mark is what the checker matches — the name
// `context` is shadowable like any other.
#[_builtin(context)]
component context<F>(default dyn) F {}

